#---
# purpose: Enum.map over two hundred thousand elements completes, because each pending continuation lives on the heap rather than the native stack
#---
# The library's map is not a tail call: every element leaves one continuation
# waiting for the rest of the list. Two hundred thousand waiting continuations
# must fit in the heap, not the native stack: a map of a hundred thousand
# elements overflows the native stack when its continuations live there.
def main() do
  mapped = Enum.map(Enum.to_list(1..200_000), fn x -> x + 1 end)
  IO.inspect(length(mapped))
  IO.inspect(hd(mapped))
  IO.inspect(hd(Enum.reverse(mapped)))
end
